{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/82373-the-triangle-of-forms","id":82373,"title":"The Triangle of Forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-01T15:43:09-08:00","id":82373,"title":"The Triangle of Forms","content":"I've always found the Lodge of Forms to spark my imagination. Their belief that there exist forms beyond the standard five is sort of confirmed by the Primal Form gift, and the way they explore the potential of their shapeshifting interests me a great deal. <br /> <br /> I've developed a kind of metaphor for the werewolf forms that I think makes sense to me, and would like to see where others might take the idea.<br /> <br /> The basic principle is that werewolf forms can be expressed in terms of their position on a three sided triangle with equal side lengths, and lines connecting the points to the center. <br /> <br /> One point is Hishu, another point is Urhan. Gauru is at the center location. Dalu is at the midpoint of the line between Hishu and Garu, and Urshil is at the midpoint of the line between Urhan and Garu. Primal form would be at the midpoint of the side connecting Urhan to the unlabeled point. <br /> <br /> The unlabeled point is a hypothetical state of existing as a pure rage monster spirit. Primal form is slightly closer to this hypothetical state than Garu is, if you look at the distances involved in the triangle, accounting for its greater destructive potential. <br /> <br /> If we assume that the nodes on this triangle that have known forms are representative, and assume that the other nodes have forms associated with them as well, we can examine the theoretical properties of the forms that exist on the unoccupied nodes. <br /> <br /> Between Hishu and Urhan would be a form that is like a kind of mini-garu, with a perfect blending of human and wolf features, but none of the monsterous characteristics of the forms closer to the rage spirit point. Given what we know about why the First Tongue is as hard to pronounce as it is, this would be an ideal form for communicating. <br /> <br /> Between Hishu and the Rage Monster apex would be a hypothetical analogue to the Primal Form, a kind of suped up Dalu form, also bigger and badder than Garu, but along the human body plan rather than the wolf body plan. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking between Garu and the Rage Monster apex we would have something very much akin to the Unihar. Raging, powerful, with only as much human or wolf features as Dalu has wolf and rage monster features, or Urshil has human and rage monster features. <br /> <br /> I can't really imagine what the Rage Monster apex would look like, since it would have to be void of human or wolf features, being a pure expression of violence and rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:45:24-08:00","id":82790,"title":"","content":"I have noticed the triangle of forms long time ago and has been mentioned by WW in the Changing breeds book as well , using the middle forms as aspects . Well the truth is that the game can be played with these three pick forms alone discarding the medial ones , but the Uratha (= wolf people) 5 forms represent the 5 faces of Luna , one form for every auspice . Hishu=Irraka , Dalu= Ithaeur , Urhan= Elodoth , Urshul=Kahalith , Gauru = Rahu . That means that the rest of the shifters are not favoured by Luna and this is why they have to work hard to gain the other 2 forms . The shapeshifting lodge , is presumed to be one that teaches how to use Mother Moon Gifts in combinations players have never imagined before , like a gauru with lion mane , or an urhan with jet black panther fur , or the eyes of a serpent , etc etc . It probably doesn't mean an overextented imbalance to these powers , but new ways on how to use them . There should have been though an extended explain on what the lodge really does . So extra dice on shapeshifting , or the boon to allow werewolves to use skins never thought they could , I believe that should have been appropriate .<br /> Now about Primal Form , well the form to me is a problem , I don't like it because it is a big tougher urshul that lacks uniqueness .It reminds me the Avatar of Wyrm from Apocalypse , with similar mechanics : Both forms have one point of attributes higher than gauru/crinos , both forms have one point of armor bonus , both forms are huge .<br /> The differences are : <b>Primal Form</b> has better regeneration than gauru , greater frenzy penalty than gauru, it may not be deactivated . <b>Avatar of Wyrm</b> does aggravated unsoakable damage with claws , like taking damage from silver , but it works against all targets .<br /> <br /> I don't believe the Primal Form should be something to mix it with the other forms , I believe though that it should be more unique . It is supposed to transform you to a prehistoric nightmare beast or something , but a huge urshul , nyaaah . I do agree though that it can be used with other Mother Moon Gifts to take various shapes . So the form has nothing to do with the shapes of wolf and man , well wolf yes , but man no . In my mind this seems somehow poor , I would prefer to see a gift that allows you to take aspects of prehistoric animals instead , or let you change size or shape ,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 03-03-2014, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}